.TH LETHEFS 4
.SH NAME
lethefs, lethed \- stateless read-only file service (Lethe)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lethefs
[
.B -A
] [
.B -D
] [
.B -C
.I kx
] [
.B -k
.I seedfile
] [
.B -u
.I user
]
.I addr
.I mtpt
.PP
.B lethed
.B -A
[
.B -v
] [
.B -a
.I addr
]
.I root
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lethe is a file protocol for static trees in which the server keeps no state
between requests: every request names its file by an absolute path, so a
server can restart, or a client move to another replica, in the middle of a
read.
It is the protocol
.B lethe1
of the Purgatorio systems, with which these programs interoperate.
.PP
.I Lethefs
dials the server at
.I addr
(default port 5640) and mounts its tree at
.IR mtpt ,
by serving Styx on a pipe; the fids Styx needs are kept by
.I lethefs
itself.
The tree is read-only.
.B -D
prints the Styx messages.
.PP
.I Lethed
serves the tree at
.IR root ,
a name in its own name space, on
.I addr
(default
.BR tcp!*!5640 ).
Requests are answered as the user
.BR none :
a file must be readable, and each directory above it searchable, by others.
.PP
By default
.I lethefs
authenticates and seals.
It signs a request for a ticket with the Ed25519 key whose 32-byte seed is in
.I seedfile
(raw, or as 64 hexadecimal digits), as
.I user
(default: the contents of
.BR /dev/user ),
and the server must trust that key.
The ticket's keys come from a hybrid exchange, X25519 with ML-KEM-768, so
that recorded traffic stays closed to someone who later breaks X25519;
.B "-C x25519"
asks for the classical exchange instead.
Every request and reply is then sealed with XChaCha20-Poly1305.
The server is not authenticated.
.PP
With
.B -A
.I lethefs
uses Lethe's clear mode instead, which has no authentication and no encryption.
.I Lethed
implements only the clear mode, and
.B -A
must be given to say so.
Neither program falls back from one mode to the other.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/lethefs.b
.br
.B /appl/cmd/lethed.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR crypt (2)
.SH BUGS
.I Lethed
issues no tickets.
.I Lethefs
does not cache: each Styx operation is one round trip or more.
It signs with a bare key only, not a certificate or a hybrid ML-DSA key,
and does not send ticket references.
